# `.agents/memory/decisions.md` is a generated router (`go run ./tools/adr index`)
# over `.agents/memory/decisions/`, and its only churn is appended table rows — one per
# new ADR. When the repo is worked in several git worktrees at once, each one adding a
# decision conflicts on that append every time, and the resolution is always "keep both
# rows". `merge=union` does exactly that automatically, which is the whole point of the
# one-file-per-decision split (see the tool's package comment).
#
# Union can duplicate a line if two branches edit the *preamble* rather than the table.
# That is not a merge to resolve by hand either: rerun `go run ./tools/adr index` and it
# overwrites the file wholesale. `go run ./tools/adr index -check` proves the committed
# router matches the files it describes, and CI runs it.
.agents/memory/decisions.md merge=union

# Go sources are LF everywhere; gofmt would rewrite CRLF anyway.
*.go text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
